cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and also cite the upstream ldpc library."
title: "qldpc_decoder_cpp: C++/HLS qLDPC decoder research scaffold"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # TODO: add ORCID when available
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/qldpc_decoder_cpp"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-26"
abstract: >-
  C++20 research scaffold for a qLDPC decoder: CMake + Catch2 + a sparse GF(2)
  mat-vec micro-benchmark, with Vitis HLS / Vivado / PetaLinux scripts targeting
  the AMD ZCU111 board. The HLS belief-propagation kernel and HIL FER verification
  are placeholders; all hardware results are UNRUN. Uses the ldpc library by
  Joschka Roffe via CMake FetchContent.
keywords:
  - ldpc
  - qldpc
  - error-correction
  - cpp
  - hls
  - fpga
references:
  - type: software
    title: "ldpc"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Roffe"
        given-names: "Joschka"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/quantumgizmos/ldpc"
